  "metadata": {
    "title": "PICES - North Pacific Marine Science Organization",
    "description": "The official data catalogue for data produced by PICES expert groups.",
    "curation_policy": "<p>Submissions are reviewed by the PICES Secretariat before publication. We accept records of data produced or assembled by PICES expert groups, projects and other PICES bodies, either as data deposits or as catalogue entries that link to data held in another repository. Each record must name its creators, carry a clear description, give the North Pacific Marine Science Organization (PICES) as publisher, and, for a catalogue entry, link to the dataset with the relation &ldquo;Describes&rdquo;. We may edit a submission&rsquo;s metadata for consistency before accepting it, and we decline submissions that are out of scope. The legacy records migrated from the former TCODE catalogue in 2026 keep the metadata of their original FGDC records.</p>",
    "page": "<h1>PICES Data Catalogue</h1>\n<p>The PICES Data Catalogue is the official catalogue of data produced by PICES expert groups, projects and other PICES bodies. It holds two kinds of record: data deposited directly in Zenodo, and catalogue entries that describe data held in national, regional or international data centres and link to them. It also holds the legacy PICES metadata catalogue formerly served by the TCODE catalogue, migrated to Zenodo in 2026. Expert groups report their data here under the PICES EG Data Reporting Protocol, following the PICES Zenodo Manual. Questions go to the PICES Secretariat at secretariat@PICES.int. The PICES official website is https://meetings.pices.int/&nbsp;</p>",
